  "worked_solution": "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{\u22c3}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}={x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=1,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}={1}\\times [-1,1]={(1,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [-1,1]}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(1,-1)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/f26fa8a525806370f5505ad097ead2b289192bb3a6eb3e341eb7c2f91a03531f.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}={i}\\times [-i,i]={(i,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [-i,i]}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,-i)$ to the point $(i,i).$ \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/bfeafe4c3b800b33b4f8550de02c2eb908effb5c28ef59b40f8c5e2bcad38ac4.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${\u22c3}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072804/assets/4d860b60ab9e139b26c9f6e1d330188d5e752a51624a2374ad713b6974e66608.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
